# ============================================================
#  Academy life — the random pool. Small moments that fill the
#  month: weather, food, money, mischief, mishaps.
#  Seasonal ones use `month` (1 Harvestmoon ... 12 Starfall).
# ============================================================

# ---------------- Around the castle ----------------

@event life_staircase
title: The Staircase Moves
class: routine
tone: light
art: tower
tags: magic
scene: A grand spiral staircase in mid-rotation, a student clinging to the banister as the steps swing toward a different floor.
text: Halfway up the west staircase, it decides to be somewhere else. You're now heading toward a floor you've never seen, at speed, and you're late for Arcana.
> left: Hold on and see where it goes
  lore +tiny
  chance 50:
    gold +small
    say: It deposits you in a dusty forgotten classroom. In a desk: eight old crowns and a love letter from 1802.
  else:
    study -tiny
    say: It takes you to the roof. Then the cellar. Then the roof again. You miss Arcana entirely.
> right: Jump for the landing
  challenge feat trivial:
    win:
      vigor +tiny
      say: You leap and land neatly. A passing portrait applauds.
    lose:
      health -small
      say: You leap and land, but not neatly. A passing portrait winces.

@event life_mystery_stew
title: Mystery Stew
class: routine
tone: warm
art: meal
tags: home
scene: A huge cauldron of grey-green stew in the dining hall, a ladle standing upright in it unaided.
text: Tonight's dinner is described on the board only as "Stew". It is grey-green. The ladle is standing up by itself. The cook is watching you with hope.
> left: Eat it bravely
  chance 60:
    health +small
    mood +small
    say: It's... delicious? Rich, peppery, faintly glowing. You go back for seconds. The cook beams.
  else:
    health -medium
    say: It's not delicious. It's not anything a stomach should know about. You spend the night regretting it.
> right: Toast and jam again
  mood -tiny
  say: You eat toast. The cook looks hurt. You feel guilty all evening.

@event life_lost_wand
title: Where Is Your Wand?
class: routine
tone: light
art: wand
tags: magic
scene: A dormitory turned upside down, clothes everywhere, a student on hands and knees peering under a bed.
text: Your wand is gone. It was on your desk. Now it isn't. Classes start in twenty minutes.
> left: Tear the room apart
  chance 70:
    say: It's in your boot. Why is it in your boot? You make it to class with seconds to spare.
  else:
    study -small
    mood -tiny
    say: You find it at lunch, inside the pillowcase. You've missed a whole morning.
> right: Try a summoning charm
  challenge spell trivial:
    win:
      arcana +tiny
      say: It flies into your hand from inside the wardrobe, offended at having been lost.
    lose:
      health -tiny
      say: Every pencil in the dormitory flies at your face. The wand stays hidden out of spite.

@event life_snoring_roommate
title: The Snorer
class: routine
tone: warm
art: bed
tags: home
scene: A dark dormitory, one bed shaking with snores so loud the curtains flutter, another occupant glaring with a pillow over their head.
text: Your roommate snores like a dragon with a head cold. You haven't slept properly in a week.
> left: Brew a silencing draught
  challenge brew trivial:
    win:
      health +small
      alchemy +tiny
      say: Perfect silence. Too perfect. Your roommate is now silent even when awake. It wears off by Tuesday.
    lose:
      health -tiny
      say: The draught makes them snore in harmony. In two voices.
> right: Move to the common room sofa
  health -tiny
  mood -tiny
  charm +tiny
  say: You sleep on the sofa and meet everyone who comes down at 3am. Some of them are very interesting.

@event life_portrait_gossip
title: The Portraits Talk
class: routine
tone: eerie
art: mirror
tags: mystery
scene: A long gallery of gilded portraits, painted figures leaning out of their frames toward each other, whispering behind painted hands.
text: Two portraits in the east gallery are gossiping about a student. Then one of them says your name and they both go suspiciously quiet.
> left: Bribe them with flattery
  challenge negotiate trivial:
    win:
      guile +tiny
      lore +tiny
      say: Ten minutes of compliments on their brushwork, and they tell you everything. Gossip about half the faculty, too.
    lose:
      mood -tiny
      say: "Flattery," sniffs the duchess, "is so common." They turn their backs. Literally.
> right: Pretend you didn't hear
  mood -tiny
  say: You walk on. Behind you, the whispering resumes, louder.

@event life_pixies
title: Pixie Infestation
class: routine
tone: tense
art: sparkle
tags: danger
scene: A dormitory full of tiny blue winged creatures swinging from curtains, stealing socks and pulling hair.
text: Someone left a window open and the dormitory is now full of pixies. They're stealing socks, unscrewing bedposts and laughing in very high voices.
> left: Fight them off
  challenge feat trivial:
    win:
      vigor +tiny
      renown +small
      say: You catch nine with a laundry bag. The dorm cheers. The pixies swear at you, colourfully.
    lose:
      health -small
      say: You lose. The pixies hang you from the chandelier by your robe. It takes an hour to get down.
> right: Bribe them with sugar
  gold -tiny
  mood +small
  say: You lay a trail of sugar cubes out of the window. The pixies follow it, munching, and leave one sock as a tip.

@event life_gargoyle
title: A Talkative Gargoyle
class: windfall
tone: light
art: tower
tags: magic
scene: A weathered stone gargoyle on a parapet, one eye open, mouth moving, a student sitting beside it with a sandwich.
text: The gargoyle above the east door clears its throat as you pass. "You," it rumbles. "You look like someone who'd listen. Nobody listens to gargoyles."
> left: Hurry along
  say: "Typical," says the gargoyle. It sulks until spring.
> right: Sit and listen
  lore +small
  mood +tiny
  say: It tells you three hundred years of academy gossip, including where the founders hid the good biscuits. You find the biscuits.

@event life_brownies
title: Help in the Night
class: routine
tone: warm
art: house
tags: magic home
scene: Tiny bearded figures in aprons tidying a cluttered student desk by moonlight, one darning a sock.
text: You wake to find your desk tidied, your socks darned and your essay proofread. Brownies. They expect something in return. Traditionally: cream.
> left: Leave out a bowl of cream
  gold -tiny
  mood +small
  study +tiny
  say: Your room stays spotless all term. Your essays have suspiciously good spelling.
> right: Leave them nothing
  alignment -tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: The next morning, every one of your socks is tied in knots. Brownies keep score.

@event life_midnight_snack
title: Midnight Hunger
class: routine
tone: warm
art: meal
tags: home
scene: A student in pyjamas tiptoeing past a sleeping prefect toward a door marked KITCHENS, a candle cupped in their hand.
text: It's midnight and you're starving. The kitchens are three floors down, past a prefect's post.
> left: Go back to bed hungry
  health -tiny
  say: You dream of sandwiches. Long, detailed, beautiful sandwiches.
> right: Sneak down (Guile)
  challenge deceive trivial:
    win:
      health +small
      mood +small
      say: Cold pie, a pot of custard, a heel of bread. Feast of kings.
    lose:
      gain detention
      say: The prefect is awake. You spend a week washing the pots you were trying to raid.

@event life_insomnia
title: The Ceiling at 3am
class: routine
tone: warm
art: moon
tags: home
scene: A student lying awake staring at a ceiling where faint painted stars have started slowly moving.
text: You can't sleep. Your brain has decided to replay every embarrassing thing you've said since you were six.
> left: Get up and study
  lore +small
  health -tiny
  say: By dawn you've read three chapters and remembered one of them.
> right: Brew chamomile and count the painted stars
  gold -tiny
  health +tiny
  mood +tiny
  say: Halfway through counting, the stars start counting back. Then you're asleep.

@event life_morning_run
title: The Dawn Run
class: windfall
tone: light
art: sun
tags: nature
when: month <= 3 or month >= 7
scene: The lakeshore path at dawn, mist on the water, a lone runner's breath steaming, the towers catching the first gold light.
text: A group of students runs the lakeshore every dawn. They've invited you. It's very early. It's very cold.
> left: Sleep in
  mood +tiny
  say: You hear them come back, glowing and smug. You are warm and unrepentant.
> right: Run with them
  vigor +small
  health +small
  mood +tiny
  say: You nearly die at the first mile and feel immortal by the third. The lake shines like a coin.

@event life_homework_mountain
title: The Pile
class: routine
tone: light
art: scroll
tags: study
scene: A desk buried under a precarious tower of scrolls and books, a student peeking hopelessly over the top.
text: Three essays, a potion log, a star chart and a reading list the length of your arm. All due this week. The pile has achieved its own weather.
> left: Grind through it
  study +small
  health -small
  mood -tiny
  say: You finish at 4am on the last day. Every piece is handed in. You sleep through breakfast.
> right: Pick what matters, skip the rest
  gold -tiny
  gain slacking
  mood +small
  say: You hand in two of five and go for a walk. The professors are not pleased. You feel great, temporarily.

@event life_stolen_answers
title: The Answers
class: routine
tone: tense
art: scroll
tags: study danger
when: month == 3 or month == 4 or month == 9 or month == 10
scene: A folded paper being passed under a library table, the faint glow of an examiner's seal on it.
text: A third-year is selling copies of next week's exam. Ten crowns. "Guaranteed real," he whispers. "Straight from the examiner's desk."
> left: Walk away
  alignment +tiny
  mood +tiny
  say: Two weeks later, five students who bought copies are suspended. The answers were fake.
> right: Buy a copy
  alignment -small
  gold -small
  chance 40:
    study +large
    guile +tiny
    say: They're real. You ace it. You also can't quite look the examiner in the eye.
  else:
    study -medium
    gain detention
    say: They're fake, and planted. You're caught with a copy. Detention, and a very cold letter home.

@event life_backfire
title: Spell Backfire
class: routine
tone: tense
art: sparkle
tags: magic danger
scene: A student mid-hiccup, a small firework bursting from their mouth, classmates ducking.
text: You mispronounce a minor cheering charm in the corridor. Something goes wrong. Every time you hiccup, a tiny firework comes out.
> left: Go to the infirmary
  gold -tiny
  say: Sister Amaranth cures it in a minute and charges you five crowns. "For the ceiling," she says.
> right: Live with it
  gain hiccup_hex
  renown +small
  say: You become briefly famous as "the sparkler". It's not the fame you wanted.

@event life_lake_swim
title: A Swim in the Lake
class: story
tone: light
art: wave
tags: nature
when: month >= 9 or month <= 1
scene: Students leaping off a wooden jetty into a sparkling lake on a hot afternoon, something large and dark moving far beneath the surface.
text: It's hot and the whole year has gone down to the jetty. Something large is rumoured to live in the deep part. People are swimming anyway.
> left: Stay on the jetty
  mood +tiny
  say: You dangle your feet and eat cherries. Something brushes your toe. You keep your feet up after that.
> right: Dive in
  health +small
  mood +medium
  chance 20:
    flag lake_knows
    say: In the deep part, you open your eyes underwater and see a round door, far below, glowing. Then you need air.
  else:
    say: The water's perfect. Something large and friendly swims under you, and you decide not to panic.

@event life_stray_cat
title: A Cat Moves In
class: routine
tone: warm
art: cat
tags: home
scene: A scruffy black cat sitting on a dormitory pillow as if it has always lived there, one torn ear, very green eyes.
text: A black cat with one torn ear is sitting on your pillow. It looks at you as though you are the one trespassing.
> left: Shoo it out
  mood -tiny
  say: It leaves with enormous dignity and moves in with your neighbour, who spoils it rotten.
> right: Let it stay
  mood +small
  gold -tiny
  say: It's called Professor now. It sleeps on your homework. You've never been happier.

@event life_storm_night
title: The Lights Go Out
class: routine
tone: eerie
art: bolt
tags: mystery
when: month >= 6 and month <= 8
scene: A dark common room lit only by lightning, students huddled under blankets, one telling a ghost story.
text: A storm knocks out every light-crystal in the dormitory. The common room fills with students, blankets and somebody's terrible ghost story.
> left: Tell an even scarier story
  challenge negotiate trivial:
    win:
      renown +small
      mood +small
      say: Your story is so good that three people sleep with the lights on for a week. You're a legend.
    lose:
      mood +tiny
      say: Your story is not scary. It is, however, accidentally hilarious.
> right: Light the room with a spell
  challenge spell trivial:
    win:
      renown +small
      arcana +tiny
      say: You fill the room with soft floating lights. Someone starts singing. It turns into the best night of term.
    lose:
      health -tiny
      say: You light the sofa. Briefly. The storm seems less frightening after that.

@event life_mirror_talks
title: The Honest Mirror
class: windfall
tone: light
art: mirror
tags: magic
scene: A bathroom mirror with a stern painted face in its silvering, frowning at a student mid-toothbrush.
text: The bathroom mirror has started commenting on your appearance. "Hair," it says this morning. Just: "Hair."
> left: Ask for its advice
  charm +small
  say: It turns out to be an excellent stylist. You look great. You hate that it's right.
> right: Cover it with a towel
  mood +tiny
  say: It sulks under the towel. Muffled: "Hair."

@event life_prank_war
title: Prank War
class: routine
tone: light
art: mask
tags: social
scene: A corridor ankle-deep in enchanted soap bubbles, two dormitories' worth of students hurling them at each other.
text: The dormitory across the corridor turned your door into a goat. The goat is fine. Honour, however, demands retaliation.
> left: Rise above it
  mood -tiny
  say: You take the high road. The goat eats your homework. You let it.
> right: Retaliate (Guile)
  challenge deceive trivial:
    win:
      renown +small
      mood +small
      say: You fill their dorm with a thousand singing bubbles. They concede by dawn.
    lose:
      gain detention
      renown +tiny
      say: You're caught carrying a crate of bubbles. Detention, but the goat seems proud of you.

@event life_mail_owl
title: The Wrong Letter
class: windfall
tone: eerie
art: letter
tags: mystery
scene: A ruffled delivery owl dropping a scented pink envelope onto a breakfast plate, a student looking up in confusion.
text: A delivery owl drops a scented pink letter in your porridge. It's addressed to someone else. It's a love letter. It's very, very passionate.
> left: Deliver it to its owner
  charm +tiny
  renown +tiny
  say: The recipient goes crimson and thanks you. Two weeks later, they're holding hands with the sender in the dining hall.
> right: Read it first
  alignment -tiny
  guile +tiny
  mood +small
  say: You read it. You will never be able to look the potions professor in the eye again.

# ---------------- Money ----------------

@event life_money_from_home
title: A Parcel From Home
class: windfall
tone: warm
art: pouch
tags: home money
when: turn >= 2
scene: A brown paper parcel tied with string on a dormitory bed, a knitted scarf, a jar of jam and a small coin purse spilling out.
text: A parcel from home: a knitted scarf, a jar of jam, a note telling you to eat vegetables, and a small purse of coins.
> left: Save the money
  gold +medium
  mood +small
  say: You tuck it away. The jam lasts six days.
> right: Spend it on a treat for your friends
  gold +tiny
  mood +medium
  charm +tiny
  say: Cake from the village for everyone. You're popular for an entire afternoon.

@event life_found_purse
title: A Purse in the Grass
class: routine
tone: light
art: pouch
tags: money
scene: A velvet purse lying in the long grass beside a path, coins glinting at its open mouth, initials embroidered on it.
text: A fat velvet purse lies in the grass by the path. Forty crowns at least. Embroidered initials: A.T.
> left: Return it to its owner
  gold -tiny
  alignment +small
  rel thorne +medium
  renown +small
  say: A.T. turns out to be Aldric Thorne. He takes the purse and stares at you a long moment. "Honest," he says. It sounds like a diagnosis.
> right: Keep it
  alignment -small
  gold +large
  guile +tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: Forty crowns richer. A few days later, Thorne mentions in class that he lost something. He looks at no one in particular.

@event life_peddler
title: The Travelling Peddler
class: routine
tone: light
art: lantern
tags: money magic
scene: A gaudy painted wagon at the academy gates, hung with lanterns and trinkets, a peddler with a gold tooth grinning.
text: A peddler's wagon has parked by the gates. "Lucky charms! Genuine article! Twenty-five crowns, and fortune follows you for a season!"
> left: Buy a lucky charm
  when: gold >= 25
  hint: 25 gold
  gold -large
  chance 50:
    gain inspired
    mood +small
    say: It's a real one. Things go right all month. You start talking to it.
  else:
    mood -tiny
    say: It turns your neck green. Fortune does not follow you. The peddler is long gone.
> right: Just browse
  mood +tiny
  say: You buy nothing and enjoy a sugared apple and the peddler's outrageous stories.

@event life_bookshop
title: Sale at Grimsby's
class: routine
tone: light
art: book
tags: money study
scene: A crooked bookshop with books stacked to the ceiling, a hand-painted sign in the window reading HALF OFF, MOSTLY.
text: Grimsby's Books is having a sale. An old copy of "Advanced Arcane Theory" for twenty crowns. Normally fifty. It's annotated, apparently, by a famous wizard.
> left: Buy it
  when: gold >= 20
  hint: 20 gold
  gold -medium
  lore +medium
  arcana +small
  say: The annotations are brilliant, rude and occasionally about the author's divorce. You learn a great deal.
> right: Leave it
  say: You walk away. You think about it for weeks.

@event life_new_robes
title: Shabby Robes
class: routine
tone: light
art: crown
tags: money social
when: renown >= 10
scene: A student in a hall mirror holding up a fraying sleeve, a tailor's flyer in their other hand.
text: Your robes are fraying at every hem. Someone at dinner called them "vintage". It was not a compliment.
> left: Patch them yourself
  mood -tiny
  charm +tiny
  say: Your stitching is crooked but cheerful. Some people start copying it.
> right: Buy new robes (30 gold)
  when: gold >= 30
  hint: 30 gold
  gold -large
  renown +small
  charm +small
  say: Midnight-blue wool, silver trim. People actually turn to look. You walk differently all week.

@event life_card_game
title: A Game of Wizard's Hand
class: routine
tone: light
art: cards
tags: money social
scene: A smoky corner of the common room, students around a low table with cards and coins, one card floating and changing face.
text: A late-night game of Wizard's Hand. The cards change faces when no one's looking. The pot is thirty crowns. The upper-years look hungry.
> left: Play (Guile)
  challenge deceive easy:
    win:
      gold +large
      say: You read every bluff and keep a straight face. Thirty crowns and a reputation.
    lose:
      gold -medium
      say: You lose fifteen crowns and the upper-years' respect, in that order.
> right: Watch and learn
  guile +tiny
  say: You learn more watching than you would have playing. Mostly about who cheats.

@event life_essay_prize
title: The Essay Prize
class: routine
tone: light
art: feather
tags: study money
scene: A brass plaque on a noticeboard announcing THE LUMEN ESSAY PRIZE — 50 CROWNS, a quill pinned beneath it.
text: The Lumen Essay Prize: fifty crowns for the best essay on "Magic and Duty". The deadline is Friday. You have an idea already.
> left: Enter
  challenge research easy:
    win:
      gold +large
      renown +medium
      say: You win. Your essay is read aloud at dinner. You don't know where to look.
    lose:
      lore +tiny
      say: You don't win, but the judges' notes are glowing. Next year, maybe.
> right: Skip it
  say: The winner reads their essay aloud at dinner. Yours would have been better. Probably.

@event life_charity
title: The Winter Fund
class: routine
tone: light
art: coin
tags: money social
when: month >= 3 and month <= 5
scene: A collection jar shaped like a lantern on the dining hall table, half full of coins, a hand-lettered sign: FOR THE VILLAGE WINTER FUND.
text: The village winter fund is collecting for families who can't afford fuel this winter. The jar is half full.
> left: Donate twenty crowns
  when: gold >= 20
  hint: 20 gold
  alignment +small
  gold -medium
  renown +small
  mood +small
  say: Your name goes on a little list by the jar. You feel warm, which is the point.
> right: Walk past
  alignment -tiny
  say: You walk past. The jar fills anyway. You think about it on cold nights.

@event life_shady_offer
title: A Quiet Job
class: routine
tone: tense
art: mask
tags: money danger
scene: A hooded figure in an alley behind the village tavern holding out a sealed envelope, a purse visible in their other hand.
text: A hooded figure behind the tavern: "Deliver this envelope to the boathouse at midnight. Don't open it. Thirty crowns." The envelope is warm.
> left: Refuse
  say: The figure melts into the dark. The next morning, someone's boat is missing.
> right: Do the job
  gold +large
  chance 40:
    gain watched
    say: You make the drop. Bram is watching from the boathouse window. He writes something down.
  else:
    guile +tiny
    say: You make the drop. Nobody sees. Thirty crowns, and a slightly cold feeling in your stomach.

# ---------------- Body & mind ----------------

@event life_food_poisoning
title: The Fish Was Off
class: incident
tone: grim
art: meal
tags: crisis
scene: A student curled on a dormitory bed clutching their stomach, a half-eaten fish pie on the bedside table.
text: The fish pie at dinner was a mistake. Your stomach is staging a revolution.
> left: Ride it out
  health -medium
  mood -tiny
  say: A miserable night. You never look at fish pie again.
> right: Get a tonic from the infirmary
  gold -tiny
  health -tiny
  say: The tonic tastes like old pennies, but it works.

@event life_self_doubt
title: Imposter
class: windfall
tone: warm
art: mirror
tags: home
scene: A student sitting alone on the edge of a fountain at night, staring at their reflection broken up by ripples.
text: Everyone around you seems to belong here more than you do. They cast faster, learn quicker, laugh easier. Maybe the letter was a mistake.
> left: Write down everything you've learned
  mood +medium
  lore +tiny
  say: The list is longer than you expected. Much longer. You pin it above your bed.
> right: Talk to someone about it
  if bonds(friend) + bonds(close) + bonds(partner) > 0:
    mood +large
    say: Your friend laughs — not at you. "You? Everyone thinks you're the one who belongs." It helps more than you can say.
  else:
    mood +small
    say: You talk to the night porter. He tells you everyone feels this way. You decide to believe him.

@event life_sleepwalking
title: Sleepwalking
class: story
tone: eerie
art: moon
tags: mystery
scene: A student in pyjamas standing on a moonlit battlement, eyes closed, one foot raised over the edge, an owl watching.
text: You wake up on the battlements in your pyjamas, at the very edge, with no memory of how you got there. Your feet are wet with lake water.
> left: Tell Sister Amaranth
  gold -tiny
  health +tiny
  say: A sleeping draught and a stern warning. It doesn't happen again.
> right: Keep it to yourself
  mood -tiny
  chance 40:
    flag lake_knows
    say: It happens twice more. Each time you're facing the lake. Each time, you're a little closer to the water.
  else:
    say: It doesn't happen again. You start locking your door from the inside, just in case.

@event life_quiet_afternoon
title: A Quiet Afternoon
class: windfall
tone: light
art: leaf
tags: nature
scene: A student lying in the long grass under an oak tree, a book open on their chest, clouds drifting above the towers.
text: For once, nothing is due, nobody needs you, and the sun is out. A whole afternoon, unclaimed.
> left: Nap under the oak tree
  health +medium
  mood +small
  say: You wake to find a bird sitting on your book. It seems content. So are you.
> right: Practise spells in the meadow
  arcana +small
  mood +tiny
  say: You make dandelion seeds dance in spirals for an hour. Nobody sees. It's perfect.

@event life_injury_stairs
title: The Trick Step
class: routine
tone: tense
art: cross
tags: danger
scene: A stone staircase with one step glowing faintly, a student mid-fall, books flying everywhere.
text: The ninth step on the north stair is a trick step. Everyone knows. You forgot. Your leg sinks to the knee and the stair holds on.
> left: Wait for someone to help
  mood -tiny
  study -tiny
  say: Forty minutes later, a first-year pulls you out. You're late for everything.
> right: Wrench yourself free
  challenge feat trivial:
    win:
      vigor +tiny
      say: You pull free with a pop. Your shoe stays in the stair forever.
    lose:
      gain injured
      health -small
      say: Something in your knee goes click. Not a good click.

@event life_lake_fever
title: Lake Fever Season
class: windfall
tone: grim
art: rain
tags: crisis
when: month >= 3 and month <= 6
scene: A dormitory where half the beds hold sniffling students with faintly blue-glowing noses, tissues everywhere.
text: Half your dormitory has Lake Fever. Noses are glowing blue. You feel a tickle in your throat.
> left: Dose up on Maud's tea
  if met(maud):
    health +small
    say: Maud's lemon-and-thunder tea keeps you upright through the whole outbreak.
  else:
    chance 50:
      gain sick
      say: The tea from the kitchens isn't the same. Your nose starts glowing on Thursday.
    else:
      say: You dodge it. Somehow.
> right: Keep going as normal
  chance 60:
    gain sick
    say: You keep going as normal for exactly two days.
  else:
    vigor +tiny
    say: Iron constitution. You sail through. Everyone hates you a little.

# ---------------- Seasons ----------------

@event life_first_snow
title: First Snow
class: routine
tone: light
art: snow
tags: nature festival
when: month == 4 or month == 5
scene: The academy courtyard blanketed in fresh snow, students mid-snowball fight, a snowman wearing a professor's hat.
text: The first snow of winter falls overnight and the whole academy wakes up giddy. Classes are optional, officially. Unofficially, they're cancelled by snowball.
> left: Join the snowball war
  mood +medium
  vigor +tiny
  chance 30:
    health -tiny
    say: You take a snowball to the face from the headmistress herself. Her aim is terrifying.
  else:
    say: Your side wins. You build a snow-fort that lasts until Thawmoon.
> right: Hot chocolate by the fire
  gold -tiny
  mood +small
  health +tiny
  say: You watch from the window, warm and smug, while the snowballs fly.

@event life_spring_cleaning
title: Spring Cleaning
class: routine
tone: warm
art: broom
tags: home
when: month == 7 or month == 8
scene: A dormitory with every window thrown open, brooms sweeping by themselves, dust swirling in sunbeams.
text: Spring cleaning. The brooms are enchanted, but the enchantment needs supervising. Your dorm's brooms have formed a union.
> left: Negotiate with the brooms (Charm)
  challenge negotiate trivial:
    win:
      mood +small
      say: You agree to one day off a week and a polish. The dorm sparkles.
    lose:
      health -tiny
      say: The brooms do not accept your terms. They sweep you into a cupboard.
> right: Clean by hand
  health -tiny
  vigor +tiny
  mood +tiny
  say: An afternoon of scrubbing. It's oddly satisfying. You find three lost quills and a sandwich from Thawmoon.

@event life_summer_heat
title: The Heat
class: routine
tone: light
art: sun
tags: nature
when: month == 10 or month == 11 or month == 12
scene: Students lying flat on the cool stone floor of a shaded colloquy, fanning themselves with exam papers.
text: The heat is unbearable. Even the gargoyles are sweating. The lake is crowded, the library stifling, the dormitories ovens.
> left: Cast a cooling charm on your room
  challenge spell trivial:
    win:
      mood +small
      renown +small
      say: Your room becomes an icebox. People pay to visit. You let them for free. Mostly.
    lose:
      mood -tiny
      say: You make it colder. Briefly. Then hotter. Then it rains inside.
> right: Sleep on the roof
  gold -tiny
  mood +small
  say: You sleep under the stars with half the dormitory. It's the best idea anyone's had all year.

@event life_harvest_festival
title: The Harvest Feast
class: story
tone: light
trigger: auto
repeat: 12
art: meal
tags: festival
when: month == 1 and turn > 1
scene: Long tables groaning under pies and roast vegetables, candles floating above, a giant pumpkin carved like the headmistress.
text: The Harvest Feast: pies the size of cartwheels, cider, and a pumpkin carved to look like the headmistress, which she pretends not to notice.
> left: Eat until you can't move
  health +small
  mood +medium
  say: You eat three helpings of everything. You're carried back to the dorm by friends. Worth it.
> right: Help in the kitchens for extra pay
  gold +medium
  charm +tiny
  say: You serve pie to the entire academy. The cooks slip you coins and a whole pie of your own.

@event life_rival_academy
title: Visitors From Thornwick
class: routine
tone: tense
art: shield
tags: rival social
when: turn >= 6
scene: A delegation of students in green robes marching through the gates, noses raised, a Lumenhold crowd watching suspiciously.
text: A delegation from Thornwick Academy is visiting. Their students are smug, polished and very loudly unimpressed with Lumenhold's plumbing.
> left: Be a gracious host
  health -tiny
  charm +small
  renown +tiny
  say: You show them the observatory. One of them admits, grudgingly, that it's better than theirs.
> right: Defend Lumenhold's honour (Arcana)
  challenge spell trivial:
    win:
      renown +medium
      say: You challenge their best to a friendly duel and win. The Thornwick students are quieter at dinner.
    lose:
      renown -small
      health -small
      say: You challenge their best to a friendly duel and lose, quite unfriendly. Thornwick will be insufferable.

@event life_lost_firstyear
title: A Lost First-Year
class: windfall
tone: light
art: compass
tags: social
when: month <= 3
scene: A tiny first-year in enormous robes standing in the middle of a junction of five identical corridors, clutching a timetable upside down.
text: A tiny first-year is standing in the middle of the corridor, clutching an upside-down timetable and trying very hard not to cry.
> left: Point the way and hurry on
  say: You point. They go the wrong way anyway. You hope they're all right.
> right: Walk them to class
  mood +small
  study -tiny
  charm +tiny
  say: You walk them all the way and they talk the entire time. You're late, but they've decided you're their hero.

@event life_frog_escape
title: The Frogs Are Out
class: windfall
tone: tense
art: frog
tags: danger
scene: A potions classroom overrun by dozens of hopping green frogs, one sitting smugly on the professor's desk.
text: Someone knocked over the frog crate in Potions. Thirty frogs are loose. One has climbed into the professor's hat. He has not noticed yet.
> left: Help round them up
  vigor +tiny
  study +tiny
  say: You catch eleven, a personal best. The professor finds the hat frog at dinner. You were not involved.
> right: Quietly let a few escape out the window
  mood +small
  guile +tiny
  say: Five frogs hop to freedom in the lake. You feel like a liberator.

@event life_fortune_teller
title: The Village Fortune-Teller
class: routine
tone: eerie
art: eye
tags: mystery
scene: A beaded doorway into a tiny dim tent, an old woman with a crystal ball and too many rings beckoning.
text: In the village, an old fortune-teller beckons you into her tent. "Two crowns for your future, dearie. Five for a good one."
> left: Pay two crowns
  gold -tiny
  chance 50:
    mood +small
    say: "You will meet a tall stranger." You already have. Several. It's an academy.
  else:
    mood -tiny
    say: "Beware of water." She won't say more. You think about the lake a lot.
> right: Pay five crowns
  gold -tiny
  mood +small
  say: Your future is wonderful. She's very specific. You are fairly sure she's making it up, and you don't care.

@event life_volunteer
title: Clean-Up Duty
class: windfall
tone: warm
art: broom
tags: home
scene: Students in rolled-up sleeves raking leaves on the great lawn, a groundskeeper directing them with a pitchfork.
text: After the storm, the grounds are a wreck. Volunteers needed to help clear branches and rebuild the hen-house. No pay. Lots of mud.
> left: Volunteer
  vigor +tiny
  mood +small
  rel maud +small
  say: A long day of mud and laughter. An old woman in a straw hat brings everyone cocoa and remembers your name.
> right: Stay in and study
  study +tiny
  say: You study through the shouting and hammering outside. The hen-house is very nice when it's done.
